WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.168 --> 00:00:03.040
- [Man] Imagine you're
driving through the hot,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.365
Moroccan desert.

00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:06.241
Your car breaks down (metal crunches)

00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:09.016
and the nearest village is 20 miles away.

00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:10.207
Would you panic?

00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:11.594
Would you give up?

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:13.307
Or would you convert
your car into a motorbike

00:00:13.307 --> 00:00:16.373
in a lengthy process that
might get you killed?

00:00:16.373 --> 00:00:21.198
Meet Emile Leray, the mechanical
magician who did just that.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:23.487
Close to a small town in
France, there is a man that

00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:24.467
loves cars.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.384
- Bonjour.

00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:29.444
- [Man] Specifically,
the French Citroën 2CV.

00:00:29.444 --> 00:00:30.386
Like those.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:34.303
("Can-Can Music" by Offenbach)

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.732
(tires screech)

00:00:42.732 --> 00:00:44.991
(whimsical music)

00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:47.030
And he's got this
funny-looking motorbike with an

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.362
extraordinary story behind it.

00:00:49.362 --> 00:00:53.195
- (speaking foreign language)

00:01:18.738 --> 00:01:21.192
- [Man] Obviously, like any
other stranded desert traveler,

00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:23.803
Emile decided to turn the
still-working parts of that car

00:01:23.803 --> 00:01:25.470
into this motorbike.

00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:28.546
First, he removed the car's frame.

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:32.379
- (speaking foreign language)

00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:41.561
- [Man] Then, he shortened
it to make a better chassis,

00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:44.514
fixed the axles, and put
the wheels on the bike.

00:01:44.514 --> 00:01:45.385
Simple, right?

00:01:45.385 --> 00:01:46.647
- No.

00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:49.263
- [Man] Oh, yeah, he also
added suspension, and, well,

00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:52.653
an engine, an ignition,
and a comfortable seat.

00:01:52.653 --> 00:01:55.776
After 12 days and 11 nights
in the desert, he was ready

00:01:55.776 --> 00:01:58.026
to go back to civilization.

00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:03.866
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:08.414 --> 00:02:10.780
- [Man] Finally, to his
delight, he came upon the police

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:13.839
who greeted him with a hefty fine.

00:02:13.839 --> 00:02:17.672
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:24.373 --> 00:02:26.823
- [Man] Back in France, the
motorcycle ended up alongside

00:02:26.823 --> 00:02:28.703
Emile's other Citroën creations.

00:02:28.703 --> 00:02:30.015
Like this boat,

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:31.695
this rugby ball,

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:34.150
a table saw, and even
glasses made out of rubber

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.271
from the seat.

00:02:35.271 --> 00:02:37.798
This guy really loves his Citroëns.

00:02:37.798 --> 00:02:39.966
Makes you wonder what's next.

00:02:39.966 --> 00:02:42.830
- (speaking foreign language)

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.663
(big band music)

